Authoritative evidence: /tmp/jev-live-cancellation-rnf8ffvx/verification-summary.json, codex-cleanup-audit.json and claude-cleanup-audit.json, manifests, approved request captures and per-fixture traces. The coordinator independently reviewed all assertions. Actual product workers (not fake) ran with mock Jev routing, no new live Gateway evaluation. Both fixtures first passed separately approved pnpm validation (3 Node tests), then user-selected and approved a real worker, saved a first edit, and received a real signal while still executing. Both stopped after two orchestration iterations and one call, retained exactly src/add.js, protected hashes unchanged, no subsequent action/late edits/live worker processes, and no emergency harness cleanup. Approved packet == trace toolInput, pre-attempt worker metadata generation0, refreshed state generation1/tests {ran:false}/repoRefreshRequired false. Codex CLI0.159.3 configured gpt-5.6-terra/high received SIGINT then SIGTERM during cleanup, CLI exit130, workerExitCode null, cancelled true/timedOut false, workerDuration14561ms, signal-to-CLI-exit1044ms. Claude Code2.1.287 configured Sonnet/medium received SIGTERM, CLI exit143, workerExitCode143, cancelled true/timedOut false, workerDuration5485ms, signal-to-CLI-exit1033ms. Local process identity/group checks found no surviving observed worker processes; do not overclaim remote model termination, all OS portability, or successful final task completion. Windows independent descendant cleanup limits remain documented.

Change: mark active cancellation milestone implementation/offline/live verification complete dated2026-10-01, add a concise exact live results table and a paragraph about saved edits, independent validation invalidation, trace/approval/process cleanup checks. Update the current pending statement that real coding-worker signal verification remains separate, while keeping prior offline/fake-worker verification clearly historical. Keep temporary paths/artifacts local (may describe artifact categories, no tracked dumps). README add a short milestone verification paragraph in appropriate existing verification/milestone section, not noisy quickstart metrics. Clarify cancellation is now completed rather than among remaining future work if a stale sentence would confuse; leave durable resume, model-tier routing, and approval automation separate.

Acceptance: correct facts match summary/audits, only these two docs modified by your task, git diff --check passes. All171 tests/check/build/mock already passed for unchanged source; do not rerun model calls, install, repeat full tests for docs-only changes, commit/push/open PR, or edit generated/local files. Follow live lifecycle preamble and report worker_done with actual changed files/checks.`;
const quote=s=>"'"+s.replaceAll("'","'\\''")+"'";
