const spec = `Target /home/peterc/jev-orchestrator branch feat/active-process-cancellation. You are Sol 6.1 medium, implementation owner. User explicitly requests commit, push and PR. All code has been root-reviewed and live verified; DO NOT modify source/docs or rerun live calls. Publish exactly the reviewed 18 files: AGENTS.md, PLAN.md, README.md, src/agents/claude.ts, src/agents/codex.ts, src/agents/types.ts, src/ai/evaluate.test.ts, src/ai/evaluate.ts, src/cli.ts, src/logging/trace.ts, src/orchestration/execute.ts, src/orchestration/loop.ts, src/process.ts, src/agents/cancellation.test.ts, src/cancellation.ts, src/cli.cancellation.test.ts, src/orchestration/cancellation.test.ts, src/process.test.ts. No generated files, traces, credentials, unrelated edits.

Current base origin/main was 9b367eecad56a82d920a1c8c5516be4b6b80667f (PR20 merge). Fetch main, verify status/diff check, stage explicit allowlist, commit title "feat: add active process cancellation", normal push -u origin feat/active-process-cancellation, then create ready PR base main titled "Add active process cancellation". Check existing PR for this head first to avoid duplicate. Do not force push, merge, manually create Entire trail/checkpoint or upgrade tools. Entire commit integration captures normally; GitHub integration attaches trail automatically. No additional user approval needed. If an unexpected file/state exists, ask coordinator before broadening scope.

PR description should lead concrete behavior: SIGINT/Ctrl+C or SIGTERM interrupts evaluation/prompts and stops active tools/workers through TERM/KILL cleanup, returns stopped, preserves partial edits, invalidates prior validation. Include separate AbortSignal outside approved request/signature, unchanged manual approvals/call/iteration limits, honest bounded schema-v2 interruption traces with null unreached stages and pre-attempt request identity; exits130/143 vs typed stop0; documented Windows descendant cleanup limitation.

Verified evidence already passed and can cite without rerunning: pnpm check, pnpm test (171 tests), pnpm build, documented mock decision smoke, git diff --check. Root independent 5 fake-process/real CLI signal fixtures passed, including approval/info prompts, partial worker edit, TERM-resistant descendant, active validation and typed stop. Real Linux/WSL live workers: Codex CLI0.159.3 configured gpt-5.6-terra/high SIGINT then SIGTERM exited130 and cleanup1.044s; Claude Code2.1.287 Sonnet/medium SIGTERM exited143 cleanup1.033s. Each 2iterations, 1worker call, cancelledtrue, non-timeout, exact saved src/add.js edit, protected fixture hashes unchanged, exact approved packet in trace, prior 3 passed tests reset and generation0->1, zero surviving observed workers and no emergency cleanup. No live Gateway evaluation in this verify. PLAN/README already record all evidence. Artifacts /tmp/jev-live-cancellation-rnf8ffvx/verification-summary.json if you need read-only corroboration, never commit artifacts.

Use gh --body-file written under .git (Snap gh cannot read host /tmp). Owner may create this local body file. Keep description concise for reviewer unfamiliar with conversation. Acceptance: commit SHA, pushed branch matching remote, PR URL+number, clean worktree, final status of checks if available; report precise error if blocked. Root will verify PR metadata and repo after worker_done. Follow injected Orca settlement obligations and check coordinator messages before done.`;
const q = s => "'" + s.replaceAll("'", "'\\''") + "'";
text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:"orca-ide orchestration worker-start --spec " + q(spec) + " --task-title 'Publish active process cancellation PR' --worktree current --agent codex --model gpt-6.1-sol --effort medium --run run_8debde958742 --timeout-ms 60000 --json", yield_time_ms:1000, max_output_tokens:3000}));

